WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:03.570
Let's go "Outfront."

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:04.771
Good evening, everyone.

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.840
I'm Kate Bolduan in for Erin

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:07.307
Burnett.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.775
"Outfront" on the front lines,

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.443
just hours from the one-year

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.711
mark of the start of Russia's

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.514
war in Ukraine, CNN has

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.416
exclusively access to one town

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:19.586
not far from where the head of

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.421
Putin's private army, the Wagner

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:22.422
group made an appearance on the

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:25.358
front lines as well.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.194
[ Speaking non-english ]

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:29.696
.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:30.430
&gt;&gt; Translator: Here and now we

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.398
can greet all men who are

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.832
fighting who are in the hospital

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.335
who are fighting for our

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:35.668
motherland.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:39.406
Volunteers who are making

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.640
ammunition.

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.442
&gt;&gt; Translator: We have seized a

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.344
five-story building close to

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:47.714
downtown bakhmut.

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.617
&gt;&gt; Translator: How far from the

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:50.917
enemy?

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:54.187
&gt;&gt; Translator: It's 400 meters.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.455
&gt;&gt; Translator: Okay, let's go.

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:56.790
Otherwise, this will be our last

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.391
address.

00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:00.527
&gt;&gt; Reporter: The danger is

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.861
certainly everywhere as the

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:05.365
brutal fighting continues there

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:05.932
without any end in sight.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.634
We're going to show you this new

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.369
video into "Outfront" showing

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.371
the utter devastation in the

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:11.704
region.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:13.373
Buildings reduced to rubble

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.942
thanks to some of the 5,000

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.744
missile strikes, 3500 air

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.814
strikes and 1100 drone attacks

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.582
that Ukraine says Russia has

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:23.383
launched over this past year of

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.717
war.

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.786
This is what some of those first

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.788
strikes looked like.

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.857
A year ago tonight in Kyiv, and

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.992
while Putin's war appears to be

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.761
grinding on at any cost in

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.397
Ukraine, he is also facing new

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.031
public opposition at home.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.532
We want to show you this.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.401
This Russian lawmakers is making

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.403
a bold mockery of Putin and

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:44.404
posting the video on YouTube.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.040
Yes, you do see him with noodles

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:48.274
hanging on his ears while

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.476
listening to Putin's big speech

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.845
this week, that act actually

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.546
demonstrates an old Russian

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.415
express which basically

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.417
translates to stop lying to me.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.719
This is a daring act by a

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.421
politician still in Russia

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.889
because we've seen many times

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:03.690
what happens to those who

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.759
publicly cross Putin.

00:02:06.893 --> 00:02:08.862
I want to go now to Alex

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:10.330
Marquardt on the ground.

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:11.698
He got an exclusive look at the

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.634
front lines, a unit made of

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.969
Americans and other foreign

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:16.369
volunteers.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.770
Alex, what did you see?

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:21.674
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Well, Kate, quite

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.009
simply total devastation.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.210
Another town in eastern Ukraine

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:24.777
lying in ruin.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:25.445
You're right.

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:28.081
We got an upclose look at

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.849
vuhledar today, a town that

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.451
Russia hopes to use to push

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:32.685
deeper into donbas but they have

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:35.455
been failing miserably raising

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.457
major questions about their

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.258
expected offensive.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:39.792
We have been speaking mostly for

00:02:39.926 --> 00:02:41.461
the past few weeks and months

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.463
about that battle for bakhmut

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.832
between Ukraine and Wagner, but

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:48.568
that is largely a symbolic

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.002
fight.

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.471
While this fight in vuhledar

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:51.905
could prove to be much more

00:02:52.038 --> 00:03:01.481
pivotal.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:02.882
On the road as the

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:06.686
sun comes up with American

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.487
fighter, Jason Mann, at the

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:07.954
wheel driving into the

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:08.621
devastating front line town

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:08.922
here.

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:09.923
Traveling in and out through a

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:10.657
muddy field means being exposed,

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.125
a direct line of sight from

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:12.926
Russian artillery and tanks.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:13.660
&gt;&gt; This is not an early morning

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:15.495
war, really, I think.

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:18.998
&gt;&gt; Reporter: First light means

00:03:19.132 --> 00:03:19.933
hopefully avoiding the endless

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:31.844
Russian shelling raining down

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.779
including terrifying

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:35.715
thermobarrack missiles.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.517
Even as Russian forces struggle

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.785
to take ground they're

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.819
inflicting damage on this town

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:40.553
which is made up of soviet era

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.521
apartment blocks blackened by

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:41.688
the fighting.

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.522
Over here a massive crater from

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.624
a Russian missile.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:45.525
Ukrainian forces do have the

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:49.529
higher ground here.

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:52.665
They are able to use these

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:53.533
buildings to defend this town,

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:54.100
but it is getting absolutely

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:54.467
pummeled.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:55.068
Only a handful of hardy

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:55.868
civilians left.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:57.971
Their home now eerie,

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:05.645
apocalyptic ruins.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:06.579
&gt;&gt; I don't like being on this

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:07.547
side.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.781
&gt;&gt; Reporter: For months Mann and

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.851
his unit of foreign troops have

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:17.790
fought alongside Ukraine's 72nd

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:19.559
brigade keeping the Russians at

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:19.626
bay.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.360
&gt;&gt; This is redefining the global

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:20.960
order as we speak.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:24.430
This is democracy versus

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:25.565
autocracy.

00:04:25.565 --> 00:04:29.569
Do we want let autocracy to

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.403
control more people's lives

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:37.577
in the future or prevent

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.212
it from ever doing that again?

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:40.546
&gt;&gt; That's what is in your head?

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:40.980
&gt;&gt; Absolutely.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:41.714
It's the only reason I'm here.

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:42.448
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Waves of Russians

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:43.149
keep coming and keep bombing.

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:43.983
This strategic corner of Ukraine

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:47.987
is where the southern and

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.589
eastern fronts meet, making it a

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:50.056
major priority for Russia's push

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.593
deeper into donbas.

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:54.293
Mann arrived in Ukraine at the

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.529
very beginning of the war.

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:57.597
He's a former U.S. Marine who

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:01.601
served in Iraq and Afghanistan

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:01.901
who went on to Columbia

00:05:02.035 --> 00:05:02.802
university and worked at Google

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:06.839
as a software engineer.

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:08.441
In the village house where the

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.410
unit lives, a few miles from the

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.611
front, Mann tells us he's now

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:16.783
here for as long as it takes.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:19.118
&gt;&gt; Ukrainians are very

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:21.621
committed to having their

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:22.255
country back, and that includes

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:22.922
crimea to most of them.

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:23.656
As long as morale is high, I'm

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.590
happy.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:25.825
&gt;&gt; Reporter: And it is, he says.

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:28.027
As the war enters its second

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:30.163
year, new recruits have also

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:30.897
just arrived from Canada and the

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:36.703
uk.

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.571
The fight so urgent, the team

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:40.039
leader, turtle, from new

00:05:40.173 --> 00:05:41.307
Zealand, only has a couple of

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.809
days to get them ready.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:46.746
&gt;&gt; And there is such a lot of

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:51.918
emotion in these fights, mainly

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.086
because from a lot of what I've

00:05:53.219 --> 00:05:54.587
seen, they don't want to be

00:05:54.721 --> 00:05:55.021
there either.

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:55.755
I never thought I'd experience

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.824
war in this sort of way because

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:58.558
we just are finding war, and I

00:05:58.691 --> 00:05:59.926
don't know, like it's like

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:00.526
fighting in a time warp.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.260
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Turtle has to head

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:03.663
to a funeral for a Ukrainian

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:04.464
teammate just killed by Russian

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:07.667
mortar fire.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:08.134
There are so many losses and

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:12.338
such little time to grieve.

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:17.110
&gt;&gt; Harder for us

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:17.777
from the foreign military,

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.780
because ever since like

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:21.681
Iraq and Afghanistan we were

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.181
losing dudes so fast all the

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:23.149
time.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:23.850
Always good to remember your

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:24.183
friends.

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:24.951
It's sad sometimes when the next

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:25.685
day you have to go and do

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:29.055
something.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:29.756
Sometimes within the same day

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:30.056
so --

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:30.823
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Both turtle and

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:31.691
Mann are very matter of fact

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:32.258
that they could lose their lives

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:33.326
fighting for a country that

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:34.961
isn't theirs.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:37.797
One year into this war, neither

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.198
is second-guessing himself.

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:39.832
&gt;&gt; Not everyone gets that

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:41.701
choice.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.370
For me it was more of a

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:45.838
serendipitous like

00:06:45.972 --> 00:06:46.873
one of those moments in your

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:48.174
life where you don't have a

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:48.775
choice.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:49.308
&gt;&gt; No regrets?

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.344
&gt;&gt; No regret, yeah.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:55.748
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Kate, Jason Mann

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:56.215
who goes by doc

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:56.783
in his unit

00:06:56.916 --> 00:06:59.118
says given the resilience and

00:06:59.252 --> 00:06:59.819
ingenuity he's seen from the

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:00.486
Ukrainians it's hard not to

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.187
believe in the Ukrainians at

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:02.789
this point.

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:03.923
Now, they are expecting some

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.858
kind of offensive by the

00:07:05.992 --> 00:07:06.592
Russians around this

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:06.993
anniversary.

00:07:07.126 --> 00:07:08.528
They don't know what is coming.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.729
They are bracing themselves

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.731
because they know how important

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:12.899
vuhledar is for the Russians in

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:14.400
their stated goal of pushing

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.169
deeper into donbas, Kate.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.270
&gt;&gt; Great to hear from them.

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:20.773
Thank you so much, Alex, for

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:21.340
bringing that to us.

00:07:21.741 --> 00:07:27.747
&gt;&gt;&gt; Now, "Outfront," foreign

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:28.347
secretary, thanks for taking the

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:28.915
time for us.

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:31.751
As we hit the one-year mark in

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:32.785
the fight the big ask from

00:07:32.919 --> 00:07:34.587
Ukraine is for fighter jets.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.755
Your former prime minister,

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:37.290
Boris Johnson actually said just

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:38.991
yesterday the uk should break

00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:41.294
the ice in his words,

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:42.395
essentially saying going first

00:07:42.528 --> 00:07:43.029
in sending jets.

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:46.966
Do you think that's a good idea?

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:51.771
&gt;&gt; Well, I pay tribute to my

00:07:51.904 --> 00:07:52.905
friend and colleague and the

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:53.773
former prime minister Boris

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:54.073
Johnson.

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:56.442
I think he was decisive in his

00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:58.144
decision-making when this

00:07:58.277 --> 00:07:59.779
full-scale invasion happened

00:07:59.779 --> 00:08:02.782
and, indeed before that in the

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.817
supplying of defensive munitions

00:08:04.951 --> 00:08:06.652
to the Ukrainian armed forces

00:08:06.786 --> 00:08:08.087
and delivering training to

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:08.955
Ukrainian troops before this

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:11.457
most recent offensive started.

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.860
And I suppose he is right that

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:15.228
we need to continue to support

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:20.766
the Ukrainians in their

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.200
self-defense.

00:08:21.334 --> 00:08:22.568
The current British prime

00:08:22.702 --> 00:08:24.770
minister has committed to

00:08:24.904 --> 00:08:26.305
training faster pilots and

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:27.807
Ukrainian Marines and, of

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:29.108
course, we will discuss with our

00:08:29.242 --> 00:08:30.710
international friends and

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:32.178
colleagues what other military

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.379
equipment the Ukrainians need

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:35.348
and how quickly we can get it to

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:35.815
them.

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:37.984
But the whole world should

00:08:38.117 --> 00:08:39.986
understand that the uk's

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:41.821
commitment with our allies to

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.956
support Ukraine is absolutely

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:44.357
unwavering.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.825
&gt;&gt; You know, Russia is making a

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:48.261
big show of it right now, of its

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:49.829
relationship with China.

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:51.364
Putin met with China's top

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:52.031
diplomat in Moscow.

00:08:52.164 --> 00:08:53.065
You also met with that same

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:54.433
diplomat in the past week, I

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:54.767
believe.

00:08:54.901 --> 00:08:56.535
The secretary of state Tony

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:58.204
blinken has said he's concerned

00:08:58.337 --> 00:08:59.839
China is considering providing

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:00.606
lethal support to Russia and

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.475
just today the German chancellor

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.010
said China sending any arms to

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:06.078
Russia would be unacceptable.

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:07.847
How likely do you think it is

00:09:07.847 --> 00:09:11.050
that China will make that move?

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:14.754
&gt;&gt; Well, I'm very, very proud of

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:16.923
the very close working

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:18.424
relationship that the uk has

00:09:18.557 --> 00:09:20.793
with yourselves and the U.S.

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:24.864
I met with Tony blinken in

00:09:24.997 --> 00:09:26.866
Munich just a few days ago.

00:09:26.999 --> 00:09:29.468
I also met with my friends and

00:09:29.869 --> 00:09:31.237
German counterparts and a number

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.306
of other foreign ministers from

00:09:33.439 --> 00:09:37.009
both Europe and further afield.

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:40.680
I completely understand why

00:09:40.813 --> 00:09:44.383
Russia would try and seek an

00:09:44.517 --> 00:09:45.217
enhanced relationship with China

00:09:45.351 --> 00:09:47.153
but the point I made to the

00:09:47.286 --> 00:09:48.688
charges authority to Wang Yi who

00:09:48.821 --> 00:09:53.359
I met with is I cannot see how

00:09:53.492 --> 00:09:56.329
it can be in China's interest to

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:57.897
import the level of criticism

00:09:57.897 --> 00:09:59.966
and international condemnation

00:10:00.099 --> 00:10:01.934
that would inevitably come with

00:10:02.068 --> 00:10:02.835
any supplying of military

00:10:02.969 --> 00:10:03.369
equipment to Russia.

00:10:03.569 --> 00:10:06.138
I can see what Russia needs from

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:06.439
China.

00:10:06.572 --> 00:10:08.341
I cannot understand what China

00:10:08.474 --> 00:10:10.242
might realistically want or need

00:10:10.376 --> 00:10:14.814
from Russia so I hope that all

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:15.414
countries uphold their

00:10:15.548 --> 00:10:17.083
obligation to the U.N. Charter

00:10:17.216 --> 00:10:18.417
and continue in this

00:10:18.551 --> 00:10:20.653
condemnation of Russia's illegal

